<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n49924" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰδοῦ</span></b> ( <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἴδου</span></b>  Hdn.Gr. ap. <i><span class="en">
			Choerob.
			<u>in Theod.</u>
			2.140
		</span></i>), aor.2 imper.
			Med.
		 of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁράω</span>; but, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰδού</span></b>  (on the accent
				v. Hdn.Gr.<i><span class="en">
				1.417
			</span></i>, al.), as Adv., <i>lo! behold!</i> (even with
			words of hearing, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰδοὺ δοῦπον αὖ κλύω τινά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Aj.</u>
					870
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.), cf.<i><span class="en">
				<u>El.</u>
				1410
			</span></i>): </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b> with Nouns
			and Prons., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰ. χελιδών</span> Klein <i><span class="en">
				<u>Meistersign.</u>
				133
			</span></i> (Attic vase, <span class="entity">vi B.C.</span>), etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰ. ἐγώ</span>
			<i>here am</i> I, <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Ge.</u>
				27.1
			</span></i>,al.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰ. ἡ μνᾶ σοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Ev.Luc.</u>
					19.20
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐκ ἰ. Ἀαρών</span>; <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Ex.</u>
				4.14
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> with Verbs,
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>a.</b> in the imper., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰ. θεᾶσθε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Tr.</u>
					1079
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ach.</u>
				366
			</span></i>; esp. in offering a thing, <i>take it</i>! 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰ. δέχου παῖ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					776
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b> in ind. of all
			tenses, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰ. πείθομαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Or.</u>
					143
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.): freq. in <i><span class="en">
				LXX
			</span></i> and <u>NT</u> with past tenses, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ge.</u>
				24.15
			</span></i>,al., <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ev.Matt.</u>
				27.51
			</span></i>, al.; in the middle of a sentence, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ev.Luc.</u>
				13.16
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> with
			questions, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰ., τί ἔστιν</span>; <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Nu.</u>
				825
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Eq.</u>
				157
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b> in repeating
			another's words quizzingly, as <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰδού γ᾽
				ἄκρατον</span> wine, <i>quotha</i>! ib.<i><span class="en">
				87
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰ. λέγειν</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				344
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰδού γε κλέπτειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Th.</u>
					206
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ec.</u>
				136
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
